{"evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_data -- --nocapture` passes (33/33), including `shipped_param_meta_loaders_return_no_diagnostics`, `shipped_source_water_presets_have_distinct_carbonate_ph`, and the updated preset metadata tests.","High-value metadata is present for several required families: process kinetics in `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml:196`, shrimp reproduction/toxicology in `crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml:92`, and source-water chemistry in `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/hard_shrimp.toml:35` and `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/moderate.toml:33`.","Denitrification has an explicit loader-layer TODO in `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml:200` and is summarized for follow-up in `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md:46`."],"findings_or_gaps":["Required carbonate-equilibrium constants are still not covered. The bead explicitly called out `pKa1`, `pKa2`, and `K_H`, but `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md:65` only summarizes source-water preset values, not those constants, and `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs:14`, `:65`, and `:73` do not provide complete provenance/confidence metadata or an explicit TODO for where that metadata will live.","The deliverable asked for coverage across habitat/biofilter scaling, but that family is still unannotated. `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md:117` lists substrate presets as not yet annotated, and representative habitat parameters such as `colonizable_area_factor` in `crates/tank_data/data/substrate/active_planted.toml:1` still have no `[param_meta.*]` entries.","The developer-facing summary is materially inaccurate for source-water metadata. `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md:67` says `hard_shrimp.toml` and `moderate.toml` annotate `bicarbonate_mg_per_l`, `calcium_mg_per_l`, and `magnesium_mg_per_l` and describes the section as heuristic, but `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/moderate.toml:33` only annotates DIC, alkalinity, and chloride, while `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/hard_shrimp.toml:55` marks calcium and magnesium as `expert`. That weakens the acceptance criterion that future maintainers can reliably distinguish strong anchors from provisional values."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Add explicit provenance/confidence coverage for `pKa1`, `pKa2`, and Henry's-law `K_H` in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` or document a clear TODO plus canonical storage location in `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md`.","Annotate at least one representative habitat/biofilter-scaling data source with `param_meta` (for example a substrate preset carrying `colonizable_area_factor` or related habitat-scaling fields), or add a bead-specific TODO that explains why the metadata cannot yet live there and where it will be recorded.","Correct `docs/PROVENANCE_STATUS.md` so its source-water table matches the actual TOML metadata coverage and confidence tiers. The summary needs to stop claiming annotations that do not exist in `moderate.toml` and stop flattening `expert` entries from `hard_shrimp.toml` into `heuristic`."],"outcome":"request_changes"}